     NetHack's dlb code was added specifically to deal with
platforms that have a severe limit on the number of files that
can be in a directory, but Windows doesn't fall into that category.
If the problem is memory corruption, switching to use nethack's
DLB configuration might make your problem seem to go away, but if
so it will just be hiding the symptom rather than fixing things.


